.TH DWSTUDIO 1 "August 2026" "vst-ace" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dwstudio \- a DW\-8000, a 4\-op FM synth, a Juno\-6 and sample kits
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dwstudio
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dwstudio
is a GTK4 window over the reimplemented engines: a Korg DW\-8000, a 4\-op FM
synth, a Juno\-6 and sample kits, voiced from banks read straight out of
plug\-in binaries rather than extracted to disk first. It hosts real plug\-ins
through the same
.B pehost
API that
.BR pestudio (1)
uses, and shares one audio graph, one keyboard and one MIDI input with them.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-dir " \fIdir\fR"
Browse this directory instead of the default corpus.
.TP
.B \-\-all
List plug\-ins that have no engine behind them as well.
.TP
.B \-\-list
Print the instruments found and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-backend " \fIname\fR"
Force an audio backend.
.TP
.B \-\-cycle " \fIms\fR"
Step through presets automatically, for demonstration.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B GDK_BACKEND
A native Linux plug\-in's editor is an X11 window and GTK hands out an X11 id
only on the X11 backend, so this wants to be \fBx11\fR under Wayland.
.TP
.B VST_ROOT
The plug\-in corpus to browse.
.TP
.BR DW_PERIOD ", " DW_LATENCY ", " DW_BACKEND
Trade latency against underruns, and pick a backend.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dw (1),
.BR peload (1),
.BR pestudio (1).
